---
title: CN Phase 2 — Ext D · HA failover at the edge
---
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant C as Client
  participant E as Edge<br/>Mac 2 · nginx
  participant A as Backend A<br/>Mac 3 · :3001
  participant B as Backend B<br/>Mac 4 · :3002

  rect rgba(37, 99, 235, 0.10)
    Note over C,B: NORMAL — round robin
    C ->> E: GET /api/status
    E ->> A: proxy_pass
    A -->> E: 200 · X-Backend: A
    E -->> C: 200 · X-Backend: A
    C ->> E: GET /api/status
    E ->> B: proxy_pass
    B -->> E: 200 · X-Backend: B
    E -->> C: 200 · X-Backend: B
  end

  Note over A: Ctrl-C — Backend A stops

  rect rgba(220, 38, 38, 0.10)
    Note over C,B: FAILURE — detected from real traffic (passive health check)
    C ->> E: GET /api/status
    E -x A: connect() → RST "connection refused"
    Note over E: max_fails=1 → A marked DOWN for fail_timeout=10s
    E ->> B: proxy_next_upstream — the SAME request, retried
    B -->> E: 200 · X-Backend: B
    E -->> C: 200 · X-Backend: B — the client never saw the failure
    C ->> E: next requests …
    E ->> B: only B while A is down
    B -->> E: 200
    E -->> C: 200 · X-Backend: B
  end

  Note over A: make backend-a — Backend A restarts

  rect rgba(13, 148, 136, 0.12)
    Note over C,B: RECOVERY — after fail_timeout nginx tries A again
    C ->> E: GET /api/status
    E ->> A: proxy_pass (probe with real traffic)
    A -->> E: 200 · X-Backend: A
    E -->> C: 200 · X-Backend: A — round robin resumes
  end

  Note over C,B: Backends are no longer a single point of failure. The EDGE still is —<br/>remove it with a floating VIP (VRRP/CARP), health-checked DNS, or the Ext E standby.
